  "supportedClaim": "Local quadratic exposure enlarges the certified decay region from alpha<6/7 at fixed layer length to alpha<3/2 when the layer shrinks sufficiently fast. An exact one-carrier bilateral lattice still carries a selected Bessel root mass asymptotic to (8/pi^2) log R inside a layer of order R^-3, so coupling dependence cannot be removed entirely."
